{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And they shall stumble, every one upon his brother.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'in the sin of his brother' — this teaches that all Israel are guarantors (ערבים) one for another. And so Moses said (Deuteronomy 29): 'every man of Israel' — all Israel are held accountable for the sin of a single man. And so you find in the case of Achan, that he was the one who sinned and all Israel were held accountable for his sin, as it says (Joshua 7): 'Israel has sinned, and they have also transgressed and also acted deceitfully and also put it among their own goods' — the sin of the individual they hung upon all Israel. And from this they said in Shir HaShirim Rabbah: 'I went down into the garden of nuts' (Song of Songs 6:11) — why were Israel compared to a nut? Just as with a nut, if you take one from the pile, all the rest roll and tumble one after another, so with Israel: if one of them is stricken, all of them feel it, as it says (Numbers 16:22): 'Shall one man sin and You be angry with all the congregation?'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:53.720733130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}